                            <comment id="17391607" author="wong" created="Mon, 2 Aug 2021 13:53:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;How soon can this issue be addressed?&#160; The current Jetty version has these CVEs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CVE-2021-28169&lt;br/&gt;
 CVE-2021-34428&lt;br/&gt;
 CVE-2021-34429&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please upgrade the jetty to 9.4.43&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17397806" author="wong" created="Thu, 12 Aug 2021 04:10:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I found a workaround to upgrade to jetty 9.4.43.&#160; I compared this jetty class against the previous version and I don&apos;t see the check for the IllegalStateException.&#160; So I built the&#160;jetty 9.4.43 locally from source with this check commented out.&#160; I then rebuilt zeppelin using my locally built jetty, and the zeppelin comes up ok.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;public class ServletHolder extends Holder&amp;lt;Servlet&amp;gt; implements UserIdentity.Scope, Comparable&amp;lt;ServletHolder&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
{&lt;br/&gt;
:   :   :&lt;br/&gt;
    private void setClassFrom(ServletHolder holder) throws ServletException&lt;/p&gt;
    {
        //if (_servlet != null || getInstance() != null)
        //    throw new IllegalStateException();
        this.setClassName(holder.getClassName());
        this.setHeldClass(holder.getHeldClass());
    }</comment>
